mangabaka_talker: guard None in _format_secondary_titles

When a MangaBaka series record has no `secondary_titles` the field comes back
as None, not as an empty dict. _format_secondary_titles iterates over
titles.values() directly, which raises AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has
no attribute 'values'. Observed against "Issak" (Vol 1). Guard the outer
iteration with `(titles or {})` — the inner `if alias is not None` guard was
already present but only protects against None items inside the dict, not
against the dict parameter itself being None.

Upstream: https://github.com/mizaki/mangabaka_talker (0.0.9, no open issue)
--- a/mangabaka_talker/mangabaka.py
+++ b/mangabaka_talker/mangabaka.py
@@ -250,7 +250,7 @@

     def _format_secondary_titles(self, titles: dict[str, list[dict[str, str]]]) -> set[str]:
         aliases = set()
-        for alias in titles.values():
+        for alias in (titles or {}).values():
             if alias is not None:
                 for a in alias:
                     aliases.add(a["title"])
